      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_89e17fa077f166df2e66095b589897b71af08ec0e99ca4947258a89797d4fb39"
      ],
      "text": "Waku is a native desktop app for working with local coding agents, built in Rust with GPUI, keeping projects, sessions, and transcripts on the user's machine."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_085b07a612db2e07162708ae125cc129b2f19a5720035fda27264efdb9064bf6",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "components",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "968d42dd38b78d28f46c36abb3d00410a4759957",
          "git_sha": "c70809ae586b8321f55427a0eec31ae87a239c3e",
          "line_end": 63,
          "line_start": 55,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "egoist/waku",
          "url": "https://github.com/egoist/waku/blob/968d42dd38b78d28f46c36abb3d00410a4759957/README.md#L55-L63"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_b557aaa132c65763866b0be86228c285a66cc91ae845830b714aef42f27a333c"
      ],
      "text": "The desktop is an RPC client of a standalone waku-daemon; provider sessions run in waku-core behind the authenticated, versioned WebSocket contract in waku-protocol, and the desktop depends on waku-client rather than the daemon implementation."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_733a5bfff9a82b89ec02f46f4ca7aeae609e783eaa1da1b668053f0b27f814d8",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "components",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "968d42dd38b78d28f46c36abb3d00410a4759957",
          "git_sha": "c70809ae586b8321f55427a0eec31ae87a239c3e",
          "line_end": 63,
          "line_start": 55,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "egoist/waku",
          "url": "https://github.com/egoist/waku/blob/968d42dd38b78d28f46c36abb3d00410a4759957/README.md#L55-L63"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_b557aaa132c65763866b0be86228c285a66cc91ae845830b714aef42f27a333c"
      ],
      "text": "The daemon owns task SQLite data, uploaded attachments, provider-native session forks, and all workspace filesystem and Git operations, while the desktop retains only presentation state and a disposable preview cache."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_046516d0660add3425b55b7835541c16fe0b6f72128e9e8531aab9679b3f8615",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "components",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "968d42dd38b78d28f46c36abb3d00410a4759957",
          "git_sha": "c70809ae586b8321f55427a0eec31ae87a239c3e",
          "line_end": 71,
          "line_start": 65,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "egoist/waku",
          "url": "https://github.com/egoist/waku/blob/968d42dd38b78d28f46c36abb3d00410a4759957/README.md#L65-L71"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_1feff8680f47f44703b548bdc949355880bce8cc291330a8fd80e48f52cd4700"
      ],
      "text": "A browser client lives at apps/web and uses a generated browser transport in packages/waku-client, with types generated from the Rust protocol and a WebSocket client implementing the same handshake, request IDs, subscriptions, deduplication, and replay cursors as the Rust client."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_403b5bd15160d4db108a59740d1c844418e7100cf38ac655c8f7bee21b37c44a",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "interfaces",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
